NOTIONAL AMOUNT

1. Definitions

In this Schedule, the following definitions shall apply:

"Notional Amount" means the specified amount on which payments and obligations under this ISDA Master Agreement and the Confirmations are based, and which shall be calculated as follows:

(a) in respect of each Transaction, the notional amount specified in the Confirmation for that Transaction;

(b) in respect of each Currency, the sum of the notional amounts for all Transactions denominated in that Currency; and

(c) in respect of all Currencies, the sum of the notional amounts for all Transactions.

2. Notional Amount

2.1 The Notional Amount for each Transaction shall be as follows:

(a) for an Interest Rate Transaction, the specified amount on which interest payments are calculated;

(b) for a Currency Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency;

(c) for a Cross-Currency Interest Rate Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency;

(d) for a FX Transaction, the specified amount in the base Currency;

(e) for an Equity Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency;

(f) for a Commodity Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency;

(g) for an Inflation Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency;

(h) for a Credit Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency; and

(i) for any other Transaction, the specified amount in the relevant Currency.

2.2 The Notional Amount for each Transaction shall be stated in the Confirmation for that Transaction and shall be expressed in the relevant Currency.

3. Examples

3.1 For example, if the Notional Amount for an Interest Rate Transaction is USD 1,000,000, then the interest payments for that Transaction will be calculated based on that amount.

