**ISDA COLLATERAL MANAGEMENT DEFINITION**

**1. INTRODUCTION**

1.1 This Collateral Management Definition (the "Definition") is an ISDA standard document that outlines the terms and conditions for collateral management in over-the-counter derivatives transactions.

1.2 This Definition is intended to provide legal definitions and provisions that govern the management of collateral, including margin calculations, eligibility criteria, and collateral valuation methodologies.

**2. DEFINITIONS**

2.1 In this Definition, the following terms shall have the meanings set out below:

(a) "Counterparty" means [Counterparty Name] or any of its affiliates.

(b) "Eligible Collateral" means any of the following assets that meet the eligibility criteria set out in Section 3:

(i) cash in the form of deposits or money market instruments;
(ii) government securities;
(iii) corporate bonds;
(iv) equities;
(v) mutual funds;
(vi) letters of credit;
(vii) commodities; and
(viii) any other assets agreed by the parties.

(c) "Margin" means the amount of collateral required to be posted or maintained by a party under this Definition.

(d) "Valuation Date" means the date on which the value of the Collateral is determined for the purposes of this Definition.

**3. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA**

3.1 Eligible Collateral shall meet the following criteria:

(a) it shall be readily marketable and capable of being sold or liquidated promptly at a price that is readily ascertainable;

(b) it shall not be subject to any lien, charge or encumbrance, other than as provided for in this Definition;

(c) it shall be free from any right of set-off or counterclaim;

(d) it shall not be subject to any restrictions on transfer, pledge or other disposition;

(e) it shall not be subject to any material tax or levy; and

(f) it shall not be subject to any material litigation, regulatory action or other material contingency.

